### YT Server API — request collection
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains' built-in HTTP client.
### Run requests top to bottom the first time; update the @variables as responses come back.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@adminAccessToken = paste-admin-access-token-here
@userAccessToken = paste-user-access-token-here
@refreshToken = paste-refresh-token-here
@videoId = paste-video-id-here
@uploadId = paste-upload-id-here
@commentId = paste-comment-id-here


### Health check
GET http://localhost:4000/health


### =========================================================
### AUTH
### =========================================================

### Login as the bootstrap admin (created via `npm run seed:admin`)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "change-me-please"
}


### Refresh tokens (rotates — old refreshToken becomes invalid)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### Logout (revokes the given refresh token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### =========================================================
### ADMIN — create the first regular user (no signup exists)
### =========================================================

### Create a creator account (admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

{
  "email": "creator@example.com",
  "password": "CreatorPass123!",
  "name": "Creator One",
  "role": "USER"
}


### Login as that new user
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "creator@example.com",
  "password": "CreatorPass123!"
}


### =========================================================
### USERS / CHANNEL
### =========================================================

### My profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### Update my channel name (avatar is a separate presign flow, see UPLOADS below)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "channelName": "Creator One Official"
}


### Update my avatar once you have a key from POST /uploads/avatars/presign
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "avatarKey": "avatars/replace-with-real-key.jpg"
}


### Public channel profile of another user
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{videoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### =========================================================
### VIDEOS — publish (after uploading bytes to S3, see UPLOADS below)
### =========================================================

### Create a video from already-uploaded S3 keys
# @name createVideo
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "title": "My First Video",
  "description": "A test upload",
  "category": "TECHNOLOGY",
  "videoKey": "videos/replace-with-real-key.mp4",
  "thumbnailKey": "thumbnails/replace-with-real-key.jpg"
}


### Edit my video's metadata
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "title": "My First Video (edited)"
}


### Delete my video (or any video, if I'm an admin)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### =========================================================
### VIDEOS — browse & watch
### =========================================================

### Home feed, most recent first
GET {{baseUrl}}/videos?page=1&limit=20&sort=recent
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### Home feed, most viewed first
GET {{baseUrl}}/videos?page=1&limit=20&sort=popular
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### Search — matches title or description, case-insensitive
GET {{baseUrl}}/videos?search=first&page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### My own uploads
GET {{baseUrl}}/videos/mine?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### Video detail (also records a view for the caller)
GET {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### Recommended videos alongside this one
GET {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}/recommended?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### =========================================================
### REACTIONS
### =========================================================

### Like a video
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}/reaction
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "type": "LIKE"
}


### Dislike a video (swaps out any existing reaction)
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}/reaction
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "type": "DISLIKE"
}


### Remove my reaction
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}/reaction
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### =========================================================
### COMMENTS
### =========================================================

### List comments on a video
GET {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}/comments?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### Post a comment
# @name createComment
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "text": "Great video!"
}


### Delete a comment (author or admin)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/comments/{{commentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### =========================================================
### UPLOADS — thumbnail & avatar (single presigned PUT)
### =========================================================

### Get a presigned URL to PUT the thumbnail image directly to S3
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads/thumbnails/presign
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "fileName": "thumbnail.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg"
}

### Then, outside this file: PUT the raw image bytes to the returned `url`,
### with header `Content-Type: image/jpeg`, and keep the returned `key` for
### the `thumbnailKey` field on POST /videos.


### Get a presigned URL to PUT a new profile picture directly to S3
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads/avatars/presign
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "fileName": "avatar.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg"
}

### Same deal: PUT the bytes to the returned `url`, then pass the returned
### `key` as `avatarKey` to PATCH /users/me (see USERS / CHANNEL above).


### =========================================================
### UPLOADS — video (resumable multipart)
### =========================================================

### 1. Initiate — server creates the S3 multipart upload and an UploadSession
# @name initiateUpload
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads/videos/initiate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "fileName": "my-video.mp4",
  "fileSize": 52428800,
  "contentType": "video/mp4"
}


### 2. Presign the parts you need URLs for (request in batches, e.g. 5 at a time)
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads/videos/{{uploadId}}/parts/presign
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "partNumbers": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
}

### Then, outside this file: PUT each part's bytes to its presigned `url`.
### Save the `ETag` response header from each PUT — you need it for `complete` below.


### 3. Resume support — ask what's already landed in S3 (after a pause/reload)
GET {{baseUrl}}/uploads/videos/{{uploadId}}/parts
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

### Compare against your total part count; presign + upload only the missing parts.


### 4. Complete — once every part has been PUT, finalize the object
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads/videos/{{uploadId}}/complete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}

{
  "parts": [
    { "partNumber": 1, "eTag": "replace-with-real-etag" },
    { "partNumber": 2, "eTag": "replace-with-real-etag" }
  ]
}

### Response includes `videoKey` — use it as `videoKey` on POST /videos.


### Abort instead (cancel the upload, e.g. user navigates away)
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads/videos/{{uploadId}}/abort
Authorization: Bearer {{userAccessToken}}


### =========================================================
### ADMIN — analytics
### =========================================================

### Per-video stats: total views, unique viewers, likes, dislikes, comments
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/videos/{{videoId}}/analytics
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}


### Views-by-day chart data (defaults to last 30 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/videos/{{videoId}}/views-by-day
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}

### With an explicit range:
# GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/videos/{{videoId}}/views-by-day?from=2026-07-01&to=2026-08-01


### Platform-wide dashboard
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}
